Game data in js/data/*.js and js/profiles.js
  These files hold item, monster and area names, item properties, text strings and drop-table
  numbers from Diablo II: Lord of Destruction and Diablo II: Resurrected. That material comes from
  Blizzard Entertainment's games and remains Blizzard's. It is NOT covered by this project's MIT
  license or by the MIT licenses quoted below, and no license from Blizzard is claimed for it. It is
  used, with attribution, in a free, non-commercial fan tool.

  Generated by tools/build-data.mjs from the JSON conversions of the game's .txt tables published
  by blizzhackers/d2data, https://github.com/blizzhackers/d2data :
    Diablo II: Lord of Destruction 1.14d  commit 9d6aea59ab7055ca6d5322fb9c7b203c1e890576
    Diablo II: Resurrected 3.3 (both rulesets)  commit fa1286949266498b294c40c2942521a7c0d7207a
  Every input file is pinned by SHA-256 in tools/sources.json. The drop rules in js/core/engine.js
  follow d2data's item-drop-spec.md at the second commit. Only the tables and columns the app uses
  are kept.

